{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/481872-advantages-for-clans-tribes-etc","id":481872,"title":"Advantages for Clans, Tribes, etc.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-15T19:49:57-07:00","id":481872,"title":"Advantages for Clans, Tribes, etc.","content":"In V:tM, every Clan or Bloodline has a weakness which in some cases helps to define that Clan. There are also optional Tribe weaknesses in W:tA which I am rather fond of. Though I have always thought it would be cool if these groups got a special advantage as well as a weakness. I know that access to their own Disciplines or Gifts is supposed to be the advantage, and that certainly is one, but I think it would be interesting if they got some additional advantage that was unique to to group in the same way that the weakness was. Has anybody ever done this before and does anybody have any ideas for what sort of advantages might be cool?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T21:39:27-07:00","id":481917,"title":"","content":"Tribal weaknesses were so optional and made so little sense that they didn't end up in W20, and even if we had an equivalent of Lore of the Clans that had something like them, I'm guessing that they probably wouldn't be the same weaknesses introduced back in the day, because of how terrible an idea those were, like instead of quirks that often plunged headlong into severely unfortunate implications that cut down the potential players below Red Talon fan numbers, they might go into more detail about Rage and how some cultural and spiritual qualities of Tribal membership might affect it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-15T21:52:12-07:00","id":481928,"title":"","content":"I actually liked the idea of Tribal weaknesses. I thought that they had the potential to add flavor to the Tribes in the same way that they added flavor to Clans in V:tM. Granted, some of them weren't that good. Like making every Silver Fang crazy, that didn't make sense. It's been forever since I've run W:tA, though if I do it again I'd likely use the weaknesses but tweak or change a fair number of them. <br /> <br /> But ultimately, this thread isn't about weaknesses, it is about advantages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T04:16:01-07:00","id":482202,"title":"","content":"Somebody just started this idea for their LARP group: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/481822-alternate-variant-clan-weaknesses\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...lan-weaknesses</a>.<br /> It contains both Weaknesses and Advantages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Currently running</u> (<a href=\"http://www.kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop\" target=\"_blank\">kpwarmerdam.nl/tabletop</a>)<br /> Helion's Advocates (MtSC)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3867-warmerdutch","name":"warmerdutch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3867_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T06:17:41-07:00","id":482268,"title":"","content":"MET had Tribal Advantages for Garou. Some of them weren't terrible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T07:20:14-07:00","id":482296,"title":"","content":"The revised-era <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/55733/Vampire-The-Masquerade-Revised-Quickstart\" target=\"_blank\">quickstart</a> had Clan advantages and disadvantages (as part of actually having a different d6-based version of the system). I think everybody in a clan having the same advantage as well as the same weakness would homogenise them too much, but the current MET <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> version with a few advantages to choose from could work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-16T08:44:06-07:00","id":482425,"title":"","content":"I think the easiest way to handle advantages if you're not feeling like making up your own, is to skim through the 2-3 dot Merits for ideas (ex: give the Nosferatu an Intimidation bonus similar to Computer Aptitude), or look to the splat books for optional things and make them free/automatic (ex: Malk Time).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-18T22:31:10-07:00","id":485122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/481872-advantages-for-clans-tribes-etc?p=482296#post482296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The revised-era <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/55733/Vampire-The-Masquerade-Revised-Quickstart\" target=\"_blank\">quickstart</a> had Clan advantages and disadvantages (as part of actually having a different d6-based version of the system). I think everybody in a clan having the same advantage as well as the same weakness would homogenise them too much, but the current MET <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> version with a few advantages to choose from could work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Those advantages are actually pretty good. I'm not sure if I like them all, but they do give me a few ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}